      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TRENTON'S MISS (2) is having her first look at this track. Comes here after a last start 4th and beaten 2.25 lengths (28.64) at Bendigo. Has never been out of the placings from two starts out of this box. Better than the latest effort and deserves another chance. HIS SPECIAL (6) is a capable type and proved too classy last time to win by 2.25 lengths at Warragul in a handy 23.12 beating Warrior Jack. Expecting another bold showing. PAW AMALFI (1) turned in a better effort at this track last start, finishing third behind Crackerjack Trev (30.68) in a Grade 5. Has the early speed to land on the pace and can stick on. Expected to be in this for a long way. AXEL'S RADAR (8) can play a role in the finish without surprising.",
